  "interpretation":[
    "The 22–30 June 1941 EAST return is a nine-day interval, whereas July–December are full calendar months. They must not be compared as equally sized months without normalization.",
    "Original German losses due to enemy action are destroyed German aircraft, not enemy aircraft claimed by German pilots.",
    "Aircraft destroyed, aircraft damaged, aircraft lost on operations for reasons other than enemy action, and aircraft destroyed not on operations are four different populations.",
    "The unit of observation is theater, month, role and damage threshold, NOT individual squadron or airfield. Source also has other monthly theaters, not yet transcribed.",
    "The original AHB translation states reports might be delayed or retrospectively revised; avoid treating its compilation month as certain plane loss event month without reviewing the underlying German returns.",
    "All numerical zeroes in these particular photographed table role cells are explicitly blank source cells interpreted as zero for that table only; never infer zero in months that have not been transcribed.",
    "Destroyed and damaged totals can include cases later recategorized; cross-check German Bundesarchiv RL 2-III and other air-force incident reports before claims-versus-loss matching."
  ]
